{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh353jYkEK13LspVzRh7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fitted Dq and B to the three spin-allowed bands, then fixed C with the spin-forbidden band. This gives **Dq ≈ 815 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 878 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 3 980 cm⁻¹**.\n\n**Approach.** Co²⁺ in KCoF₃ is high-spin d⁷, so its ground state is ⁴T₁g(F). The energies of the quartet states do not depend on C. That means the three spin-allowed bands set Dq and B, and the doublet band ²T₁(2) is then used to find C.\n\n**1. Spin-allowed bands give Dq and B.**\n- The ⁴A₂ and ⁴T₂ bands differ by exactly 10Dq. From 15 200 − 7 150 = 8 050 cm⁻¹, a first estimate is Dq ≈ 805 cm⁻¹.\n- A least-squares fit of all three quartet bands (⁴T₂, ⁴A₂, ⁴T₁(P)) to the full d⁷ energy matrices gives **Dq = 815 cm⁻¹ and B = 878 cm⁻¹**.\n\n| Band | Calculated (cm⁻¹) | Observed (cm⁻¹) | Calculated − observed (cm⁻¹) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ⁴T₂ | 7 086 | 7 150 | −64 |\n| ⁴A₂ | 15 231 | 15 200 | +31 |\n| ⁴T₁(2) | 19 199 | 19 200 | −1 |\n\nThe root-mean-square error of the fit is about 41 cm⁻¹.\n\n**2. The spin-forbidden band gives C.** I held Dq = 814.5 cm⁻¹ and B = 878.1 cm⁻¹ fixed and varied only C.\n- With C = 4 499 cm⁻¹ (the program's default value), ²T₁(2) comes out at 22 690 cm⁻¹.\n- With C = 4 000 cm⁻¹, ²T₁(2) comes out at 21 193 cm⁻¹.\n- So this level moves about 3.0 cm⁻¹ for each cm⁻¹ change in C.\n- Shifting C to match the observed 21 130 cm⁻¹ gives **C ≈ 3 980 cm⁻¹**. This value comes from interpolating between those two points; I did not run a separate check at 3 980.\n\nThis gives C/B ≈ 4.5. B is about 15% lower than for the free Co²⁺ ion, which is the small reduction expected for the fairly ionic bonding to fluoride.\n\n{\"Dq\": 815, \"B\": 878, \"C\": 3980, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Quartet bands fix Dq and B; the 2T1(2) band at 21130 cm-1 fixes C.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":n